      "g5prime_ruling": "Director adjudication r#51 §3(b) (capx-director-ledger-2026-08.md §0av): the CAP-BOUND form of G5′ ('STOP if the cap does NOT bind in a year') is VOID as a STOP and RECLASSIFIED to REPORTED, on the documents — D64 §2.3 says verbatim 'a year converting materially below the cap would be the informative surprise, not a STOP', so the source had already decided this outcome was reported, and Addendum C promoted §2.4's hour-ceiling census cell into a floor on a solved quantity. The CEILING form on ercot/pjm/miso is untouched — a published ceiling is a legitimate upper bound.",
      "mechanism_reading": "Host exhaustion, predicted by k and by nothing else. Both RGGI ISOs start cap-bound at MW-weighted k ≈ 1.0 and unbind exactly as the surviving host pool moves past k > 1.2 (NEISO 0.9952 → 1.3032; NYISO 1.0544 → 1.2235), while CAISO — the third carbon-priced ISO, armed identically — never leaves k 1.03–1.08 and stays cap-bound (96.4 % in 2030). CAISO is the CONTROL CASE: the efficient hosts are consumed first and the expensive tail cannot carry the accurate per-tonne cost, so the unbinding is a fleet-composition effect, not a level effect and not an ISO quirk."
